class:: TCauchyRand
summary:: Triggered Cauchy-distribution sampler
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Distributions
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/TStableRand, Classes/TGaussRand

description::

Uses the inverse transform code::location + abs(scale)*tan(pi*(U-0.5)):: with an open uniform variate. The Cauchy distribution has no finite mean or variance.

Extreme finite values are expected and may require explicit user-side limiting before direct audio use. Like link::Classes/TGaussRand::, it samples and holds on triggers; unlike it, TCauchyRand has a much heavier tail and local resettable seed.

subsection:: Distribution shape

image::cauchy-density.png#Centered Cauchy densities with scale = 0.5, 1, and 2, shown in muted teal, blue, and plum over a deliberately finite display interval. Larger scale lowers the center and puts more probability in the heavy tails.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: location
Center of the distribution.
argument:: scale
Cauchy scale; magnitude is used.
argument:: trig
Resample on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore the seed and sample a new initial value.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TCauchyRand.kr(0, 1, Impulse.kr(4)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(TCauchyRand.kr(500, 100, Impulse.kr(8)).clip(80, 4000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

